= V1 subject and composition migration =

The complete V1 page-role pass separates historical artifact role from the subject signal carried inside the artifact.

Only two V1 Main pages are currently first-class subject canonicalization candidates:

# <code>Bioluminescent Organisms</code>
# <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs</code>

A second set of reusable fragments carries meaningful Concept, Method, Protocol and evidence signal.

This is enough to test the V2 decomposition, but not enough to freeze the full ontology vocabulary.

== Why this page does not publish the subjects yet ==

Historical V1 text is source material. Canonical V2 subject publication requires revision comparison, citation recovery, factual revalidation, epistemic qualification and a deliberate decision about which authored formulations remain current.

Creating a polished Main page before doing that work would confuse migration progress with epistemic review.

The present step therefore records the '''mature representation target''' while preserving the archive as authority for the historical body.

== Subject candidate: Bioluminescent Organisms ==

The V1 parent page presents a coherent Biology-oriented subject and composes multiple child pages through transclusion.

The archive contains six child-page titles in the family:

* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Overview</code>
* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Biochemical Mechanism</code>
* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Mechanism</code>
* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Examples</code>
* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Applications</code>
* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms/Related Theories</code>

The parent visibly transcluded Overview, Biochemical Mechanism, Examples, Applications and Related Theories. The parallel <code>Mechanism</code> child is therefore a lineage/duplication question rather than evidence that both should survive as separate V2 Book Matter units.

=== Historical signal ===

* V1 presentation: <code>Concept Type: Idea</code>;
* API identity category: <code>Ideas</code>;
* Domain/category: Biology;
* historical status language: theoretical;
* composed parent/child structure;
* relation to Fluorescent Coral Reefs.

=== Mature V2 target ===

'''Primary modeled identity:''' likely <code>Concept</code>, subject to canonicalization review.

'''Domain:''' Biology is directly supported by V1 organization; additional domains should require content evidence.

'''Composition:''' preserve one coherent parent knowledge object. Reusable mechanism/examples/applications/theory material may remain headings or become transcluded units only where reuse/provenance/retrieval justifies independent composition.

'''Epistemics:''' do not translate V1 “Theoretical” mechanically into a page-wide V2 status. Bioluminescence as a biological phenomenon and speculative applications/theories within the page can have different evidentiary standing.

'''Relationship:''' preserve the historical connection to Fluorescent Coral Reefs, but choose a precise V2 relation only after the modeled objects are clarified.

== Subject candidate: Fluorescent Coral Reefs ==

The V1 parent presents an engineered/research project concept assembled from four transcluded children:

* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs/Overview</code>
* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs/Genetic Engineering</code>
* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs/Environmental Applications</code>
* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs/Implementation Challenges</code>

=== Historical signal ===

* visible label: <code>Implementation Type: Project</code>;
* API identity category: <code>Implementations</code>;
* historical development language: active development;
* Biology category;
* relation to Bioluminescent Organisms;
* explicit engineering/application/challenge composition.

The apparent Implementation ↔ Project conflict is productive evidence. V1 was trying to encode both '''what the effort is organizationally''' and '''what it does as an implementation'''.

=== Mature V2 target ===

'''Primary modeled identity:''' <code>Project</code> is the leading migration candidate if the page models the research/development effort. <code>Implementation</code> should remain available for a concrete implemented system/artifact when one exists.

This avoids using multiple type labels to encode distinct jobs. A Project may [[Property:Implements|implement]] a Concept/Protocol/design, produce an Implementation, use a Technology, or contain Methods without becoming all of those as its primary identity.

'''Domain:''' Biology is historically supported; Engineering/Technology or other domains should be assigned only if the canonicalized content genuinely spans those fields.

'''Epistemics vs lifecycle:''' “Active Development” is lifecycle/project state, not evidence that the underlying biological/engineering claims are Established. V2 must keep those dimensions separate.

'''Historical existence vs present status:''' V1 documents the project concept as it existed in the archived corpus. V2 must not assert that a real-world development program is currently active without current first-party evidence.

